<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sauli Niinistö</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sauli Niinistö (born 1948) is a Finnish politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-coalition-party">National Coalition Party</a> who served as president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> from 2012 to 2024. Earlier he was finance minister from 1996 to 2003, during the recovery from a deep recession and the introduction of the euro, and speaker of parliament. In his second term he led Finland into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>, which it joined in April 2023 after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s full-scale invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p></div>
